message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata. The accompanying paper will be added here when it is published."
title: "Multi-criteria selection of anomaly detection models for payment transactions: code and results (v2.0)"
type: software
version: 2.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-07"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ihor1sh/cbdc-anomaly-detection-framework"
abstract: "Corrected pipeline, raw per-run results and reproduction scripts for a pilot study that selects anomaly detection models for payment transactions by recall at a fixed false-alarm budget, AUC-PR, single-transaction latency and stability of local explanations (Elliptic Bitcoin graph as a stand-in for CBDC data). Supersedes v1.0."
keywords:
  - anomaly detection
  - model selection
  - Pareto front
  - explanation stability
  - graph neural networks
  - central bank digital currency
